+# The row was already a ring — 25 September 2026
+
+`ca_rule_explorer#study:neighbours#room:ring` extends the existing neighbour study in this map only. The explorer remains the sole automaton. Its `_grid`, current state, rule, seed, stepping and wrap code are untouched. NeighbourStudy attaches the opt-in ring and refreshes its readout through its existing refresh path.
+
+Thirty-two columns wrap around a 1.65 m radius. The lowest band, 2.02 m above the floor, is current. Up to twenty-three older rows stand above it at .095 m intervals; no uncomputed row is shown as a dead generation. The 768-instance MultiMesh copies the explorer's alive/dead colours. STEP, RUN, SEED, RST and the rule controls act on the same stored data. CELL carries the existing pink/gold triplet across the seam. Number labels face inward; they have no mirrored back face. The ring is a visual receiver and introduces no collision, sensors, controls or second clock.
+
+The map moves only the explorer: (10,4) to (10,5), with the same height, yaw and existing configuration plus `room:ring`. The baseline position overlapped the museum entrance wall: the interaction pointer could still press buttons through geometry. The revised standing approach is clear of that wall. The ring occupies the corridor beyond the desk, centred near map (10,7.1); its placement compensates for the desk's one-cell move. All nine authored works, structure cells and utilities remain.
+
+Current native review, before/after photographs and test report: `doc/book/iterations/2026-09-25-ca-neighbour-ring/index.html`. The first baseline assertion counted generated museum fixtures as authored works; the report includes all nine actual placements and that mistaken assertion is retained. The initial interaction run correctly exposed the entrance-wall obstruction. Final checks and limitations are reported on the review page. No tracked headset comfort, learner or Quest acceptance follows from supplied desktop-body and pointer tests.
+
+The manuscript gains a spatial encounter after its existing wrapped-boundary paragraph and corrects the mistaken NEXT button name to STEP. Prior code excerpts, artifact returns, references and ending are retained. Ring height represents past generations, not a second spatial dimension of the automaton. The visitor can stand inside its representation without becoming a neighbour in the update rule.
+
+---
